# Names are full English words (PR #1188, R1188-U4): file names, variables
# and functions, as the links notation we own already is (R1188-U6).
#
# The abbreviation list and the proper terms (ai, api, json and the other
# established acronyms that are not abbreviations of a word the reader would
# say) are stated once, in data/meta/notation-rules.lino; this file says where
# the rule applies to code. scripts/measure-abbreviations.mjs measures it
# against data/meta/abbreviation-ratchet.lino (gate check-abbreviations), and
# its --propose prints the full-word spelling of every abbreviated file name,
# which data/meta/rename-map.lino applies tree by tree.
#
# A file name is abbreviated when a word of its stem (the base name before
# the first `.`, split at `-` and `_`) is on the list: formal_ai_worker_nl_tools
# holds nl, natural-language. A binding is abbreviated when a word of a
# declared name (split at `_` and at a lower-to-upper case change) is on the
# list: `const args`, `let pos`, `fn calc_total`.
abbreviation-rules
  abbreviations-from data/meta/notation-rules.lino
  file-names
    excluded dev/log
      reason "evidence logs, named by the run that wrote them"
    excluded docs/case-studies
      reason "captured evidence, named by the tool that captured it (pr-1188-review-comments.json)"
    excluded changelog.d
      reason "changelog fragments, named once by their author and removed at release"
    excluded data/cache
      reason "a cache keyed by the external word it describes (wordnet id, mb, spec)"
    excluded data/view
      reason "views keyed by the external word they describe, like data/cache"
    excluded rust/embedded
      reason "a byte mirror whose names follow the originals; the rename tool moves it with them"
    excluded ts
      reason "the generated twins of js/, renamed with their sources"
    excluded data/meta/self-ast
      reason "the census of rust/src, named for the source files"
    excluded data/meta/worker-line-budget
      reason "one shard per browser worker module, renamed with it"
    excluded rust/tests/fixtures/js-rust-translation
      reason "projections of js/agentic, named for the source modules"
    excluded experiments/formal_ai_subagent/archive
      reason "the coordination archive keeps its names as written"
    excluded data/meta/requirement-status-ledger
      reason "generated, one file per requirement document and named for it"
    fixed-name lib
      reason "the stem of the crate root file Rust fixes (src/lib.rs), and of a script directory's lib.sh by the same convention"
  bindings js
    excluded js/vendor
      reason "third-party code, kept byte for byte"
  bindings rust/src
